{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Carrion and torn flesh.</b> The verse speaks of the carcass of a clean bird and of consecrated meat that went outside its precinct. Because it was permitted to them similar to carrion, such as in the case of melikah, Scripture warned that if a clean bird of non-sacred status was slaughtered by melikah it is carrion, and meat that went outside its precinct is called טרפה, as is derived for us: ובשר בשדה טרפה לא תאכלו, in the chapter בהמה המקשה. And so Ezekiel said: כל נבלה וטרפה מן וגו׳ לא יאכלו הכהנים."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:15.950071369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}